IMPORT prelude

-- Amusement Rides Safety Act 2011 (Singapore) -- what counts as an amusement ride (s 2), who is the "person responsible" (s 2), the
-- conditions for operating a ride lawfully (s 13), the term of an operating permit (s 15), ride managers (ss 16, 17), the permit
-- holder's safety duty and stop directions (s 18), lapse and revocation of the operating permit (s 22), maintenance (s 31),
-- closure for safety (s 35), adverse incidents (s 54), the penalties in Parts 2 to 8 and the general penalty (s 56), the defences
-- in ss 19(3) and 59(2), and composition (s 62).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 18/12/2023), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/ARSA2011.txt. The revised edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December
-- 2021"; the latest amendment annotated is Act 23 of 2023 (wef 18/12/2023), which touches only the building-plan approval steps
-- in ss 6 and 24 (not encoded here).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0063 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a
-- sharper question yet. SCOPED to what an operator, a ride manager, a premises owner and a rider meet. Not encoded: installation
-- and modification permit procedure (ss 5-12, 23-30, beyond their penalties), relocation (s 34), the fire and rescue management
-- system (Part 6), qualified persons (Part 7), enforcement powers (ss 48, 50-53), evidence, forfeiture, service, appeals to the
-- Minister (s 69), exemptions (s 70), and everything left to regulations (major amusement rides, insurance minimum limits, compoundable offences).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Amusement Rides Safety Act 2011 -- operation`

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the lower of` a b MEANS
    IF a AT MOST b THEN a ELSE b

§§ `2 -- what is an amusement ride`

-- s 2(1) "amusement ride": "any mechanised or power-driven device ... which (a) is designed to carry patrons on, along, around, over
-- or through a fixed or restricted course, or within a defined area, for the primary purpose of giving those patrons amusement,
-- pleasure, thrills or excitement; and (b) is available for use by members of the public upon their payment of a fee or otherwise,
-- whether or not [it] is erected to remain as a lasting part of any premises or is regularly relocated, and (c) includes such other
-- device ... as may be prescribed ...; but (d) does not include any (i) coin-operated ride; (ii) playground equipment; or (iii)
-- device ... prescribed as not being an amusement ride".
-- "power-driven" "does not include being driven solely by human physical effort". "coin-operated ride": "(a) is fixed to a
-- non-moving base; and (b) upon the insertion of any coin, slug, token, plate or disc, operates as a ride for children".
-- "playground equipment" includes "swings, seesaws, stationary spring-mounted animal features, rider-propelled merry-go-rounds,
-- climbers, slides, trampolines and physical fitness devices".
DECLARE Device HAS
    `mechanised or power-driven` IS A BOOLEAN
    `driven solely by human physical effort` IS A BOOLEAN
    `designed to carry patrons on a course for amusement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `available to members of the public` IS A BOOLEAN
    `fixed to a non-moving base` IS A BOOLEAN
    `operates as a children's ride on inserting a coin or token` IS A BOOLEAN
    `playground equipment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `prescribed to be an amusement ride` IS A BOOLEAN
    `prescribed as not being an amusement ride` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN d IS A Device
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a coin-operated ride` IF
    d's `fixed to a non-moving base` AND d's `operates as a children's ride on inserting a coin or token`

-- Reading "mechanised or power-driven" with the definition of "power-driven": a device moved only by its riders is treated here as
-- not mechanised or power-driven. That the exclusion reaches "mechanised" too is an inference; the text defines only "power-driven".
GIVEN d IS A Device
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an amusement ride` IF
        (    (    d's `mechanised or power-driven`
              AND (NOT d's `driven solely by human physical effort`)
              AND d's `designed to carry patrons on a course for amusement`
              AND d's `available to members of the public`)
         OR  d's `prescribed to be an amusement ride`)
    AND (NOT `is a coin-operated ride` d)
    AND (NOT d's `playground equipment`)
    AND (NOT d's `prescribed as not being an amusement ride`)

§§ `2 -- the person responsible`

-- s 2(1) "person responsible": "(a) the person who holds the operating permit in respect of the amusement ride; or (b) if no person
-- holds an operating permit ... for the time being -- any of the following persons: (i) the owner of the amusement ride or the
-- person who has the charge, management or control of [it]; (ii) the owner of the premises on which [it] is installed; (iii) [the
-- holder of a Public Entertainments Act 1958 licence for the approved place where it is installed]; (iv) the person who is allowed
-- by virtue of section 75 to operate the amusement ride without an operating permit; or (v) any other person ... prescribed".
-- Section 75 is not in the 2020 Revised Edition: the Comparative Table lists 2012 Ed. ss 75 and 76 as "[Omitted as spent]".
DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `the operating permit holder`
    `the owner of the ride`
    `the person in charge of the ride`
    `the owner of the premises`
    `the public entertainment licensee for the approved place`
    `a ride manager`
    `a patron`

GIVEN `the role` IS A Role, `someone holds an operating permit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a person responsible` IF
    IF `someone holds an operating permit`
    THEN CONSIDER `the role`
         WHEN `the operating permit holder` THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER `the role`
         WHEN `the owner of the ride` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `the person in charge of the ride` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `the owner of the premises` THEN TRUE
         WHEN `the public entertainment licensee for the approved place` THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `13 -- operating lawfully`

-- s 13(1): "A person must not operate an amusement ride unless (a) the person holds a valid operating permit and operates the
-- amusement ride in accordance with the conditions of the operating permit; and (b) at all times when the amusement ride is being
-- operated (i) [it] is in a state of good repair and safe working condition, and is fit for operation; (ii) there is in force a
-- certificate of compliance in respect of the fire and rescue management system ...; (iii) there is in force an insurance covering
-- the person responsible ... against liability for any injury to, or the death of, any person ... in an amount that is not less
-- than the prescribed minimum limits; and (iv) there is appointed ... at least one ride manager".
-- (The prescribed minimum limits are in regulations not retrieved; the insurance is a flag here.)
DECLARE Operation HAS
    `holds a valid operating permit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `within the permit conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in good repair and safe working condition` IS A BOOLEAN
    `fire and rescue certificate of compliance in force` IS A BOOLEAN
    `liability insurance at the prescribed minimum in force` IS A BOOLEAN
    `ride managers appointed` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN o IS AN Operation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the operation is lawful` IF
        o's `holds a valid operating permit`
    AND o's `within the permit conditions`
    AND o's `in good repair and safe working condition`
    AND o's `fire and rescue certificate of compliance in force`
    AND o's `liability insurance at the prescribed minimum in force`
    AND o's `ride managers appointed` AT LEAST 1

§§ `15 -- term of an operating permit`

-- s 15(1): an operating permit "(a) is valid ... for such period, not exceeding 12 months starting on the date of its issue, as may
-- be specified in the operating permit; and (b) may be renewed upon its expiry".
GIVEN `months since issue` IS A NUMBER, `months specified` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the permit is still within its term` IF
    `months since issue` LESS THAN `the lower of` `months specified` 12

§§ `16 -- ride managers`

-- s 16(2): when a ride manager vacates the appointment, "(a) both the holder of the operating permit and the ride manager must each,
-- within 14 days after the vacation of the appointment, notify the Commissioner"; and the holder must "(i) without delay appoint
-- ... another ride manager" and "(ii) within 7 days thereafter, notify the Commissioner of that substitute appointment".
-- (3): if the departing manager "is the only ride manager", the holder "must not commence or ... must immediately cease the
-- operation ... until [it] has appointed a substitute ride manager ... and notified the Commissioner".
GIVEN `days after the vacancy` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the vacancy notice is in time` IF
    `days after the vacancy` AT MOST 14

GIVEN `days after the substitute appointment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the substitute notice is in time` IF
    `days after the substitute appointment` AT MOST 7

GIVEN `managers remaining` IS A NUMBER, `substitute appointed` IS A BOOLEAN, `substitute notified to the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the ride may keep running after a ride manager leaves` IF
        `managers remaining` AT LEAST 1
    OR  (`substitute appointed` AND `substitute notified to the Commissioner`)

§§ `18 -- stop directions`

-- s 18(2): the Commissioner may direct the holder to cease operation and take remedial measures, "and the operation of the
-- amusement ride must not be resumed without the written consent of the Commissioner". (5): failing to comply, or resuming
-- "without the written consent of the Commissioner", is an offence ($50,000 or 6 months).
GIVEN `a stop direction was given` IS A BOOLEAN, `the ride was resumed` IS A BOOLEAN, `written consent was given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `resuming is an offence` IF
    `a stop direction was given` AND `the ride was resumed` AND (NOT `written consent was given`)

§§ `22 -- lapse, revocation and suspension of an operating permit`

-- s 22(1): the permit "automatically lapses (a) if the holder ... (i) dies, is wound up or otherwise dissolved ...; or (ii) ceases to
-- be the operator of the amusement ride; (b) if the insurance required under section 13(1)(b)(iii) ceases to be in force".
-- (2)(a): the Commissioner may revoke if "the amusement ride (not being an amusement ride that is capable of being relocated) has
-- not been in operation for a continuous period of more than 3 months". (4), (5): no revocation or suspension without a hearing,
-- unless the holder is bankrupt or in liquidation, a receiver is appointed, the holder is convicted of an offence under the Act or
-- of fraud or dishonesty, or the fire and rescue certificate has been withdrawn under s 37.
DECLARE Event IS ONE OF
    `the holder dies`
    `the holder company is wound up`
    `the holder stops operating the ride`
    `the liability insurance lapses`
    `the ride is idle for four months`
    `the holder is convicted of an offence under the Act`

GIVEN `the event` IS AN Event
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the permit lapses automatically` IF
    CONSIDER `the event`
    WHEN `the holder dies` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the holder company is wound up` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the holder stops operating the ride` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the liability insurance lapses` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `idle months` IS A NUMBER, `capable of being relocated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `idleness permits revocation` IF
    (NOT `capable of being relocated`) AND `idle months` GREATER THAN 3

GIVEN `bankrupt or in liquidation` IS A BOOLEAN, `receiver appointed` IS A BOOLEAN, `convicted under the Act or of dishonesty` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `fire certificate withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may revoke without a hearing` IF
    `bankrupt or in liquidation` OR `receiver appointed` OR `convicted under the Act or of dishonesty` OR `fire certificate withdrawn`

§§ `35 and 54 -- closure and adverse incidents`

-- s 2(1) "adverse incident" includes "(a) any malfunction ...; (b) any accident arising from the operation ...; (c) any occurrence of
-- fire ...; (d) the collapse, breakage, dislodgement or disengagement of any structure or component ...; (e) any occurrence ...
-- that results or is likely to result in (i) any injury to, or the death of, any person who is using or operating, or in the
-- vicinity of, the amusement ride; or (ii) any person being stranded or trapped".
-- s 54(1): "The person responsible for an amusement ride and the ride manager ... must, as soon as practicable, upon the occurrence
-- of any adverse incident ..., inform the Commissioner". (5): $50,000 or 6 months.
-- s 35(1): the person responsible "must wholly or partially close or cordon off the amusement ride whenever such action appears
-- reasonably necessary (a) for the safety of persons ...; or (b) in the case of the occurrence of any adverse incident".
DECLARE Occurrence IS ONE OF
    `a control system malfunction`
    `a patron injured by a restraint`
    `a small fire in a gondola`
    `a car detaching from the track`
    `riders stranded at the top`
    `a near miss likely to have injured a bystander`
    `a long queue`
    `a patron feeling dizzy after a normal ride`
    `a scheduled closure for cleaning`

GIVEN `the occurrence` IS AN Occurrence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an adverse incident` IF
    CONSIDER `the occurrence`
    WHEN `a long queue` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a patron feeling dizzy after a normal ride` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a scheduled closure for cleaning` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the role` IS A Role, `someone holds an operating permit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `must report an adverse incident` IF
    `is a person responsible` `the role` `someone holds an operating permit`
    OR  CONSIDER `the role`
        WHEN `a ride manager` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the occurrence` IS AN Occurrence, `closure appears reasonably necessary for safety` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the ride must be closed or cordoned off` IF
    `is an adverse incident` `the occurrence` OR `closure appears reasonably necessary for safety`

§§ `19(3) and 59(2) -- defences`

-- s 19(1): a permit holder or ride manager who "knows or ought reasonably to know of any contravention ... relating to the operation
-- of the amusement ride" must notify the Commissioner "as soon as practicable". (3): "It is a defence ... for the person charged to
-- prove ... that the person did not know and could not reasonably have discovered the contravention".
GIVEN `knew or ought to have known` IS A BOOLEAN, `notified` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved could not reasonably have discovered it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing to notify a contravention is an offence` IF
    `knew or ought to have known` AND (NOT `notified`) AND (NOT `proved could not reasonably have discovered it`)

-- s 59(2): where a thing must be done by the person responsible or the ride manager "and there is more than one", it is a defence
-- "for the accused to prove (a) that that thing was done by another person responsible ... or by another ride manager ...; or (b)
-- that any notice or order ... was served on another ... and not on the person charged".
GIVEN `more than one person responsible or ride manager` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved another did it` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proved the notice was served on another and not on the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the shared-duty defence succeeds` IF
    `more than one person responsible or ride manager`
    AND (`proved another did it` OR `proved the notice was served on another and not on the accused`)

§§ `Penalties (ss 5, 13, 16-19, 23, 31-33, 35, 49, 54-56)`

-- Maximum penalties on conviction, as stated in each section. Where the section provides for a continuing contravention it adds "an
-- additional fine not exceeding $X for each day or part of a day during which the contravention continues", and a further fine for
-- each day after conviction. A zero below means the section provides no daily fine.
DECLARE Penalty HAS
    `maximum fine` IS A NUMBER
    `maximum imprisonment in months` IS A NUMBER
    `daily fine while continuing` IS A NUMBER
    `daily fine after conviction` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `installing without an installation permit`
    `operating outside section 13`
    `ignoring a cessation notice`
    `operating without a ride manager`
    `a permit holder not notifying a ride manager vacancy`
    `a ride manager neglecting duties`
    `breaching the duty to operate safely`
    `defying a stop direction`
    `not notifying a contravention`
    `major modification without a permit`
    `failing to maintain the ride`
    `ignoring a repair notice`
    `minor modification without notice`
    `not closing an unsafe ride`
    `not notifying a closure`
    `giving false information`
    `not reporting an adverse incident`
    `obstructing an enforcement officer`
    `an offence with no penalty expressly provided`

-- s 5(2), 13(2), 23(2): $200,000 or 2 years; $1,000 a day; $2,000 a day after conviction.
-- s 18(4), 31(2): $100,000 or 12 months; $500 a day; $1,000 a day after conviction. s 49(1): $100,000 or 12 months.
-- s 16(4), 17(2), 32(3), 33(3): $50,000 or 6 months; $500 a day; $1,000 a day after conviction.
-- s 13(4), 18(5), 35(3), 54(5), 55: $50,000 or 6 months.
-- s 16(6), 19(2), 35(4), 56: $20,000 or 3 months.
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A Penalty
`the penalty for` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `installing without an installation permit` THEN Penalty 200000 24 1000 2000
    WHEN `operating outside section 13` THEN Penalty 200000 24 1000 2000
    WHEN `major modification without a permit` THEN Penalty 200000 24 1000 2000
    WHEN `breaching the duty to operate safely` THEN Penalty 100000 12 500 1000
    WHEN `failing to maintain the ride` THEN Penalty 100000 12 500 1000
    WHEN `giving false information` THEN Penalty 100000 12 0 0
    WHEN `operating without a ride manager` THEN Penalty 50000 6 500 1000
    WHEN `a ride manager neglecting duties` THEN Penalty 50000 6 500 1000
    WHEN `ignoring a repair notice` THEN Penalty 50000 6 500 1000
    WHEN `minor modification without notice` THEN Penalty 50000 6 500 1000
    WHEN `ignoring a cessation notice` THEN Penalty 50000 6 0 0
    WHEN `defying a stop direction` THEN Penalty 50000 6 0 0
    WHEN `not closing an unsafe ride` THEN Penalty 50000 6 0 0
    WHEN `not reporting an adverse incident` THEN Penalty 50000 6 0 0
    WHEN `obstructing an enforcement officer` THEN Penalty 50000 6 0 0
    WHEN `a permit holder not notifying a ride manager vacancy` THEN Penalty 20000 3 0 0
    WHEN `not notifying a contravention` THEN Penalty 20000 3 0 0
    WHEN `not notifying a closure` THEN Penalty 20000 3 0 0
    OTHERWISE Penalty 20000 3 0 0

-- The most a court may fine for one conviction covering a contravention that continued for a number of days before conviction:
-- the fine plus the daily fine for each day or part of a day. (Reading the daily fine as cumulative with the fine is an inference
-- from "additional".)
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `days continuing` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for` MEANS
    (`the penalty for` `the offence`)'s `maximum fine`
    PLUS (`the penalty for` `the offence`)'s `daily fine while continuing` TIMES `days continuing`

§§ `62 -- composition`

-- s 62(1): the Commissioner may compound an offence "which is prescribed as a compoundable offence by collecting ... a sum not
-- exceeding the lower of the following: (a) one half of the amount of the maximum fine that is prescribed for the offence; (b)
-- $5,000". (2): on payment "no further proceedings are to be taken". Which offences are compoundable is left to regulations.
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most a composition can be` MEANS
    `the lower of` ((`the penalty for` `the offence`)'s `maximum fine` DIVIDED BY 2) 5000
